A reader's supplement on the arcs main changed at Review 80 (agy-002's). Five of the six findings are not
checked by main. The sixth, the orders of the image at (8), is computed by main and holds, by main's table;
the orders are computed again here by main's own functions in the lock.

NO STATEMENT OF THE MATHEMATICS IS WRITTEN BY THIS PATCH. Each note is one of three texts of main's, placed
where it was missing: main's correction of 2026-11-11 as it stands at the head of B736's consolidation
page; main's sentence that withdraws the gloss, as B734's page has it; main's sentence of the orders, from
its table. Every sentence that was on a page or in a script stays as it was written.

  4  B732, its page: a line under the opening says how to read the rest. (The closing paragraph was marked
     by part 3's first patch.)
  5  B733, its page: a note under the closing paragraph, for the door at (8) named there and in the opening.
     The finding also names line 4 of the arc's script of growth; nothing about the knot's level is there
     (it names the door at 4), and the one "(8)" of that script is a ring's name. Sent back.
  6  B942, its page: the orders, and which of the two the page quotes. Part 3's second patch had said
     "in the quotient by every central unit of square one"; that agrees with main's numbers.
  8  B1067, its page: under the line that calls the result by the withdrawn gloss, that it is withdrawn.
     B736's consolidation page, where the gloss stands twice: at its head, and beside each place.
  9  B736: main's correction on the arc's own page, under the section that names the group, and at the head
     of its two scripts, as comments; and
     that the group of order 30720 which the arc writes as PSL(2, O₃/(8)) is the quotient by all eight
     units of square one. The sealed preregistration and the kept outputs are not touched.
  10 B779: main's correction at the head of the two siblings that had none, a page and a script.

THE LOCK (the test of B734, to which four tests are added under a dated note; none of main's is changed):
  - the orders are computed and the sentence built from them is main's sentence, character for character;
  - each of the ten files holds its sentences; taking any one out is reported (21 planted cases);
  - the scripts under the arcs are swept as the pages are: none states the old level without the correction
    but three cells of other arcs, held by name as found and not read by this patch. The three scripts of
    this patch were among them before it. Planted: a script as B736's stood, with its twin and two controls.

A FAULT OF THIS PATCH'S OWN, FOUND AT ITS EXPORT AND MENDED BEFORE IT WAS SENT: the note on B736's page was
first placed at the page's head. The atlas reads a page's first 1,500 characters for the tag it guesses from
words, and the note moved B736's tag from dead to banked. The note now stands under the section it is about,
the page's first 1,500 characters are as they were, and the atlas's data are unchanged by this patch. The
lock holds that. It goes back to main: a note placed at the head of any page can move that tag.

MEASURED AND NOT MENDED: beside the scripts, 18 kept outputs and files of results in 10 arcs state the old
level with no correction. A kept output is what a run printed. Whether such a file is to carry a note is
main's.

The tests of B732, B733, B734, B736, B779 and B942 pass: 36 before the four, 40 with them. Tested against planted
errors by the session that wrote it.
